 {
  "kind": "text",
  "text": "I've built the 12-second scene in the Main comp. I checked it on a contact sheet at ten timestamps. I haven't played it back in real time, so the jitter and the sucking-in motion are unchecked.\n\n- **Beat 1 (0–4s):** Six sticky notes in yellow, pink, mint, orange, blue and lilac pop in one after another, each with a different password. They jitter through 4s using a rotation-wiggle expression. I haven't confirmed that expression produces visible jitter. The shield fades in behind the pile from 3.2s, so there's no cut.\n- **Beat 2 (4–7s):** The notes spin and shrink into the shield one after another. The shield pulses each time one lands, then does a final lock-in squash at about 6.5s.\n- **Beat 3 (6.4–12s):** A flat cyan glow disc blooms behind the shield, which rises slightly as the glow grows. \"One key. Every login.\" slides up at 7.5s. A white check mark then draws itself onto the shield at 8.2s. The glow pulses gently until the end.\n\nBeat 3 starts earlier than a strict 4s split (about 6.4s rather than 8s), so the lock-in doesn't sit idle.\n\nAt 5.4s a small white fragment shows near the shield. I think it's note text mid-suck, but I didn't confirm it isn't the check mark.\n\nI can make the beats an even 4s each, or give the glow a soft gradient instead of the flat disc.",
  "at": 1794501818330
 },
